# =====================================================================================
# vector_space_law.rq — RED->GREEN probe for T-VECTORSPACE (the FIELD-SCALARS tooth, W2 · SP0).
# Re-homes fnd:VectorSpaceAxiomsShape / q_vectorspace_axioms (basicttl/foundation/algebra_rings.ttl:270-273,
# 204-208,581) — restricted to its distinguishing field-scalars requirement — into the folded stratified
# idiom, over the vector-space model's declared scalar structure (@rel:scalar:field = the scalar structure,
# typed @typ:field:scalar:structure when it is genuinely a field).
# =====================================================================================
# The VECTOR-SPACE field-scalars law (the scalar ring is a FIELD — the sole law a vector space adds over a
# module): a vector-space model's declared scalar structure (@rel:scalar:field) must be a field-typed
# structure (@typ:field:scalar:structure). This SELECT returns every (model, scalarStructure) for which the
# scalar structure is NOT a field-typed structure — i.e. the scalars are drawn from a mere ring, so the model
# is a MODULE, not a vector space.
#
#   GREEN (a genuine vector space, e.g. fixtures/vector_space_pos.ttl — the 1-dimensional space {V0,V1,V2}
#         over the GF(3) FIELD, scalar structure typed @typ:field:scalar:structure): 0 rows — the scalar
#         structure is a field, satisfied.
#   RED   (a broken vector space, e.g. fixtures/vector_space_neg.ttl — the scalar structure retyped
#         @typ:ring:scalar:structure): >= 1 row — the declared scalar structure is a non-field ring, so the
#         field-scalars law fails and the tooth bites.
#
# Run over the algebra data graph merged with the fixture under test, inference=none. Companion SHACL:
# shapes/vector_space.shapes.ttl VectorSpaceScalarFieldShape (sh:targetClass rec:model:record) carries the
# SAME clause, so the runner's fixture iteration catches the negative through the shape too. NOTE the INHERITED
# module scalar-action typing law (probes/module_law.rq) still applies — a vector space IS a module — and is
# satisfied in BOTH polarities of this fixture pair (the scalar actions land in V in pos and neg); ONLY this
# field-scalars probe flips.

PREFIX rel: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:>
PREFIX typ: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:type:>

SELECT DISTINCT ?model ?scalarStructure WHERE {
  # a vector-space model's declared scalar structure
  ?model rel:scalar:field ?scalarStructure .
  # the scalar structure is NOT a field-typed structure: the scalars are not drawn from a field
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?scalarStructure a typ:field:scalar:structure .
  }
}
